 "note": "Quick, Draw! palm tree 6535444676214784, seen from below as in the film. Strokes 0, 8 and 9 are the trunk: an inner line, an inner box and the outer tapering trunk. Strokes 1 to 7 are seven fronds drawn as closed leaf loops that all start at the top of the trunk: 1 the long frond to the right, 2 up and to the right, 3 the big frond to the left, 4 straight up, 5 up and to the left, 6 low to the left, 7 low to the right. The whole drawing is placed by two points, the top of the trunk where the fronds meet (crown) and the foot of the trunk (base). The trunk does not bend. Each frond turns a few degrees about the crown by its own sway angle, measured from the movement of the matching frond in the footage, so the fronds stir in the wind at the frames the film's fronds stir.",
